Problem: The figure below shows a grid of $10$ squares in a row. Each square has a diagonal connecting its lower left vertex to its upper right vertex. A bug moves along the line segments from vertex to vertex, never traversing the same segment twice and never moving from right to left along a horizontal or diagonal segment. Let $N$ be the number of paths the bug can take from the lower left corner ($A$) to the upper right corner ($B$). One such path from $A$ to $B$ is shown by the thick line segments in the figure. Find $\sqrt{N}$.

[asy]
size(12cm);
draw((0, 0)--(0, 1));
for (int i = 0; i <= 9; i += 1)
{
draw((i, 1)--(i + 1, 1)--(i + 1, 0)--(i, 0)--(i + 1, 1));
}
draw((0, 0)--(0, 1)--(2, 1)--(2, 0)--(3, 1)--(3, 0)--(4, 1)--(4, 0)--(5, 0)--(5, 1)--(6, 1)--(6, 0)--(7, 1)--(8, 1)--(8, 0)--(10, 0)--(10, 1), red + linewidth(2));
label("$A$", (0, 0), dir(180));
label("$B$", (10, 1), dir(0));
[/asy]

