Solution: The number of $1\times1$ squares in the diagram is $2(n-1)$, the number of $2\times 2$ squares is $n-2$, and the number of $\sqrt{2} \times \sqrt{2}$ squares is also $n-2$ (see diagram).  Solving \[
2(n-1)+n-2+n-2=70
\] we find $n=\boxed{19}$.

[asy]
unitsize(5mm);
defaultpen(linewidth(.7pt)+fontsize(8pt));
dotfactor=4;

int i,j;

for(i=0;i<=10;i=i+1)

for(j=0;j<=2;j=j+1)

{

dot((i,j));

}

draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,1)--(0,1)--cycle);
draw((3,0)--(5,0)--(5,2)--(3,2)--cycle);
draw((7,1)--(8,2)--(9,1)--(8,0)--cycle); [/asy]
